<title>LUXEMBOURG: France urges EU to increase food market share.</title>
<headline>France urges EU to increase food market share.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>European farmers must continue to produce enough food not only for Europe but also for expanding non-European markets, France's new agriculture minister Louis Le Pensec said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's our task to guarantee consumers secure food supplies,&quot; Le Pensec told a meeting of EU farm ministers.</p>
<p>At present about 20 percent of farmers, mostly the largest and wealthiest, receive 80 percent of EU farm aid.</p>
<p>&quot;More freedom should be given to member states to modulate EU aid,&quot; Le Pensec said, referring to the adjustment of aid according to farm size.</p>
<p>On Friday, EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler had also called for a fairer allocation of EU farm aid.</p>
</text>
